# Pre-Submission Checklist

Before saving and submitting any prediction file, verify all of the following:

## Format
- [ ] Columns are exactly: `student_id`, `career_success_score`
- [ ] Row count matches `test.csv` exactly
- [ ] No NaN or Inf values in predictions
- [ ] Predictions are clipped to [0, 100]

## Validation
- [ ] CV MSE has been printed and recorded
- [ ] OOF predictions match expected distribution (roughly 0–100)
- [ ] No features computed from the full train+test set (leakage check)

## File Naming
- Save as: `data/submissions/submission_{tag}_{cv_mse:.4f}.csv`
- Example: `data/submissions/submission_lgbm_xgb_ensemble_12.3456.csv`

## Kaggle Limits
- Daily limit: **5 submissions**. Use them deliberately.
- Track every submission in a comment or experiment log.

## Code to validate:
```python
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

sub = pd.read_csv("data/submissions/submission.csv")
assert list(sub.columns) == ["student_id", "career_success_score"]
assert not sub["career_success_score"].isna().any()
assert sub["career_success_score"].between(0, 100).all()
print(f"Submission valid. Shape: {sub.shape}. Score range: [{sub['career_success_score'].min():.2f}, {sub['career_success_score'].max():.2f}]")
```
